  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>Saily</strong> if you'd normally pay for a VPN or ad-blocker when traveling anyway and want one eSIM that keeps working as you cross borders. Pick <strong>AloSIM</strong> if you want a free international phone number bundled in and the choice of a fixed-GB or unlimited plan from the same provider. Both are priced close enough that the 15% code each one offers matters more than the sticker price.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: A Security Suite vs. A Free Phone Number</h2>
  <p>
    Saily is NordVPN's eSIM spin-off, built by the same company (Nord Security), and every plan ships with ad blocking, malware/phishing site blocking, and a virtual-location tool included. It also sells one universal eSIM that keeps working as you cross into a new supported country, rather than a separate profile per region.
  </p>
  <p>
    AloSIM's point of difference is a free international phone number through a partnership with Hushed, set up separately inside the AloSIM app after you buy a plan. It's not a swap for your real number, but it's useful for receiving a verification text or giving out to a hotel abroad. AloSIM also sells both fixed-data and unlimited plans on its own site, so you get that choice without switching providers.
  </p>

